  "description": "Qwen3 Embedding 0.6B served by the already mirrored official vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 OpenAI-compatible image in pooling runner mode. This Forge fallback profile was added after both TEI CUDA 1.9.3 and TEI CUDA 12.9 revision 5bc4d88 failed on B300/SM103. The upstream public Hugging Face model metadata reports Apache-2.0 licensing, no gating, 595,776,512 BF16 safetensors parameters, sentence-transformers feature-extraction usage, and text-embeddings-inference compatibility. The current vLLM 0.21 pooling documentation lists OpenAI-compatible `/v1/embeddings` for embedding usage and says to run pooling models with `--runner pooling`; Hugging Face discussion #50 for this Qwen model also updates vLLM usage from `task=\"embed\"` to `runner=\"pooling\"`. Forge uses the same vLLM CUDA 13 digest that already validated B300 for Qwen3 4B text generation. A 2026-05-24T00Z retained B300 diagnostic proved the earlier manifest arg `--task embed` is rejected by the vLLM 0.21 CLI before server startup, so this profile now uses `--runner pooling`. Corrected 2026-05-24T00Z probes returned HTTP 200 from `/v1/embeddings` and completed 3 warmups plus 10 measured embedding requests on all five Forge GPU cells: B300/uk-south1, B200/us-central1, H200/eu-north2, L40S/eu-north1, and RTX6000/us-central1. A 2026-05-24T01Z L40S direct-pod parity check compared the full 1024-dimensional embedding vector against the TEI CUDA 1.9.3 row for the default manifest prompt and measured cosine similarity 0.999921044, mean absolute difference 0.000307053, and max absolute difference 0.002205543. This manifest is now an active, testing, non-default, non-latest publication candidate; keep default_eligible=false because TEI remains much cheaper on non-B300 cells and B200 vLLM startup is still node-cache dependent.",
